WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.164
Module three:

2
00:00:01.164 --> 00:00:02.543
centralized exchanges.

3
00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:07.429
How the order book works, what fees really cost, what futures and funding are,

4
00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:11.438
and why leverage liquidates you even when the forecast is right.

5
00:00:12.438 --> 00:00:14.627
Nobody sets the price on an exchange.

6
00:00:14.627 --> 00:00:15.988
There is an order book:

7
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:18.414
a list of those who want to buy and sell.

8
00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:21.076
Sellers are at the top, buyers at the bottom,

9
00:00:21.076 --> 00:00:24.034
and the gap between the best prices is the spread.

10
00:00:24.034 --> 00:00:26.460
A limit order sits in the book and waits.

11
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.134
A market order takes the best orders one after another until it fills its size.

12
00:00:32.134 --> 00:00:35.109
In the lesson you can get your hands on the order book:

13
00:00:35.109 --> 00:00:38.300
send a market order and see at what average price it fills.

14
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.519
The bigger the order compared with the depth of the book, the worse the price.

15
00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:43.438
That is slippage.
